[OPT_READER]
\par \--reader=STRING
Force reading of the audio file (if any) by the reader with the specified id.
Specifying an unavailable reader or a reader unable to read the input file will
result in an error.
\n\n
The following readers are available with the current version of libarcsdec:
\htmlonly
<table class="m-table">
	<tr> <th>ID</th>                  <th>Description</th> </tr>
	<tr> <td><tt>wavpcm</tt></td>     <td>Internal RIFF/WAV reader for PCM encoded audio. Fast, but experimental.</td>   </tr>
	<tr> <td><tt>ffmpeg</tt></td>     <td>Reader for WAV,FLAC,APE,CAF,OGGFLAC,AIFF and ALAC in M4A based on ffmpeg.</td> </tr>
	<tr> <td><tt>flac</tt></td>       <td>Reader for FLAC based on libFLAC.</td>                                         </tr>
	<tr> <td><tt>wavpack</tt></td>    <td>Reader for .wv container based on WavPack.</td>                                </tr>
	<tr> <td><tt>libsndfile</tt></td> <td>Reader for WAV,FLAC and AIFF based on libsndfile.</td>                         </tr>
</table>
\endhtmlonly
\manonly
.sp
.TS
tab(|);
ll.
ID         | Description
---------- | -----------
wavpcm     | Internal RIFF/WAV reader for PCM encoded audio. Fast, but experimental.
ffmpeg     | Reader for WAV,FLAC,APE,CAF,OGGFLAC,AIFF and ALAC in M4A based on ffmpeg.
flac       | Reader for FLAC based on libFLAC.
wavpack    | Reader for .wv container based on WavPack.
libsndfile | Reader for WAV,FLAC and AIFF based on libsndfile.
.TE
.sp
\endmanonly
[OPT_READER]

